# generated/

`@SLUG@_generated.c` is **ROM-derived**: the C the recompiler emits for the
instructions the harvester actually saw execute in your own dump of @NAME@. It
is produced on your machine by `cmake --build build`, and it is gitignored.

**Never edit anything in this directory.** Family law, and the reason is
practical rather than stylistic: the file is regenerated from the ROM on every
pipeline run, so an edit here survives exactly until the next build and then
disappears — taking whatever it fixed with it. Fix the recompiler, the runtime,
or `game.toml`, and regenerate.

Whether this directory is ever committed is the open distribution-posture
question recorded in `../docs/STATUS.md`; until that is decided it stays local,
which is the reversible choice.
